The <ansi fg="command">combatstats</ansi> command can be used in the
following ways:

<ansi fg="command">combatstats summary</ansi>
Display the combat analytics dashboard.

<ansi fg="command">combatstats summary [type]</ansi>
  e.g. <ansi fg="command">combatstats summary spell</ansi>
Filter the dashboard by attack type.

<ansi fg="command">combatstats types</ansi>
List all attack types in the current buffer.

<ansi fg="command">combatstats matchups</ansi>
Show PvM / MvP / PvP / MvM event breakdown.

<ansi fg="command">combatstats defense</ansi>
Show dodge / parry / block success rates.

<ansi fg="command">combatstats position</ansi>
Show hit rates by target position and grapple status.

<ansi fg="command">combatstats reset</ansi>
Clear the combat event buffer.

<ansi fg="command">combatstats export</ansi>
Flush current buffer to the analytics log file.
